meta {
  name: List Products
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products?_fields=sku&_fields=status
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Accept: application/json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.data: isArray
  res.body.pagination: isDefined
}

docs {
  `GET /api/v3/products` — search, filter, and page through products. All query
  parameters (`_fields`, `_page`, `_page_size`, `_sort_by`, filter params) are
  undeclared in `openapi_pimv3.json` but confirmed working live (2026-09-04/07
  against "David's Dev Account"). See `config/api-testing.config.md` quirks #7-13.

  ## This resolves the v3-unreachable blocker
  v3 is live and matches its documented shape. It was unreachable earlier only
  because it was tested against the wrong host/account (`pim.plytix.com` under the
  "API Docs" account) — v3 for this engagement is served from a separate DEV
  host/account. See `config/api-testing.config.md` for the full history.

  ## Spec discrepancy — missing query parameters
  `openapi_pimv3.json`'s `GET /api/v3/products` declares **zero** query params.
  All of the following work live and must be flagged to Plytix:
  - `_fields=<field>` (repeatable): sparse field selection.
  - `_page` + `_page_size`: page-number pagination. Default page size is 25.
  - `_sort_by=<field>`: ascending sort.
  - `<field>=<value>`: plain field equality filter (e.g. `sku=BAG-10157`).
  - `<field>[<op>]=<value>`: operator filter (e.g. `created[gt]=2026-01-01`).
  - `<related>.<field>=<value>`: related-entity dot filter (e.g. `categories.name=Backpacks`).
  - `attributes.<name>=<value>` / `attributes.<name>[<op>]=<value>`: custom attribute filters.

  ## `_fields` / `_expand` edge cases
  - `_fields=category_ids` **400s** (`HiddenFieldError: Field 'category_ids' does not
    exist in model 'Product'`). Use `_fields=categories` — returns fully expanded
    category objects.
  - `_fields=relationships` is **silently dropped** (200, field absent). The real
    field is `product_relationships`.
  - `_expand=<relationship>` **400s** (`InvalidFieldError`). Expansion is automatic
    per `_fields` value — no `_expand` needed.

  ## Pagination (confirmed 2026-09-07, re-verified and extended 2026-10-01)
  - Default page size: 25. `pagination.next_page` is a full URL (link style).
  - `_page` + `_page_size`: works (see Pagination example below).
  - `_offset` + `_limit`: **400** `InvalidFieldError` — not supported on this resource.
  - **Bounds (new 2026-10-01)**: `_page` must be >= 1 and `_page_size` <= 1000.
    Both enforced as `422 InputDTOValidationError` naming `query._page` /
    `query._page_size` — the only query params in this project confirmed to
    carry real server-side validation bounds.
  - **`_total_count` and `_filtered_count` do NOT exist (new 2026-10-01)**:
    both return `400 {"name":"InvalidFieldError","description":"Field
    '_total_count' does not exist."}`. They appear in `API V3.md`'s prose but
    were never implemented. There is **no count of any kind** available from
    this API — the only way to size a result set is to page to the end and
    tally, or request `_page_size=1000` and read `data.length` when the set is
    known to be small. Confirmed on `/products` and `/assets`.
  - **Pagination keys are OMITTED, never null (new 2026-10-01)**. The spec's
    `Pagination` schema declares both as `string | null`, but live:
      - first page of a multi-page set -> `{"next_page": "..."}` only
      - a middle page -> both keys
      - the last page -> `{"previous_page": "..."}` only
      - a single-page result set -> `{}` (empty object)
      - a page past the end -> `200`, `data: []`, `{"previous_page": "..."}`
      - single-resource `GET /products/{id}` -> no `pagination` key at all,
        and `data` is an object, not an array
    Any client doing `if (res.pagination.next_page !== null)` is wrong; test
    for presence/falsiness instead.
  - **⚠️ `next_page`/`previous_page` are `http://` URLs (new 2026-10-01).**
    They 301-redirect to `https://...:443`, and many HTTP clients drop the
    `Authorization` header across a scheme-changing redirect — plain
    `curl -L` on the returned URL yields `401 {"detail":"Unauthorized"}`.
    `curl -L --location-trusted` (or rewriting the scheme to `https`) works.
    This is a real hazard for the "just follow the URL" guidance. Report to
    Plytix as a link-generation bug.

  ## Filter dialect
  `API V3.md` lists a JSON-object "Current" syntax and a query-string "Possible
  Alternative". v3 implements the **query-string** dialect. Confirmed live: plain
  field (`sku=BAG-10157`), operator (`created[gt]=2026-01-01`), related-entity dot
  (`categories.name=Backpacks`), custom attribute (`attributes.brand[icontains]=Plytix`).

  ## ⚠️ Preferred way to get expanded categories/assets/static_lists (2026-09-23)
  The dedicated subpaths (`GET /products/{id}/categories`, `.../assets`,
  `.../static_lists`) are confirmed BROKEN as of 2026-09-23 -- always empty
  regardless of real linkage. `_fields=categories`/`_fields=assets`/
  `_fields=static_lists` on THIS endpoint is the confirmed correct way to get
  the same expanded data. See "200 - Full Parameters (Relationship Fields
  Expanded)" below, and `Get Product Subpath - Attributes.bru` for the full bug
  writeup.

  See examples below for representative responses for each scenario.
}

example {
  name: 200 - Sparse Field Selection
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-04. Two _fields params return only sku and status per product; pagination.next_page carries the cursor forward.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products?_fields=sku&_fields=status
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [
            {
              "id": "6a38f614c3d65a5f868b1a06",
              "sku": "BAG-10157",
              "status": "Completed"
            },
            {
              "id": "6aa022262b6fd055ffb7caa4",
              "sku": "WC-TEST-FULL-001",
              "status": null
            }
          ],
          "errors": [],
          "pagination": {
            "next_page": "http://pim.dev.plytix.com/api/v3/products?_fields=sku&_fields=status&_page=2"
          }
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: 400 - _total_count / _filtered_count Do Not Exist
  description: Confirmed live 2026-10-01. Both count parameters described in API V3.md are rejected outright. Identical response for _filtered_count, and identical on /assets — this is not a products-only gap. There is no count mechanism in this API.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products?_total_count=true&_page_size=2&_fields=sku
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 400
      text: Bad Request
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [],
          "errors": [
            {
              "name": "InvalidFieldError",
              "description": "Field '_total_count' does not exist."
            }
          ]
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: 200 - Last Page (previous_page only, next_page key absent)
  description: Confirmed live 2026-10-01. Account holds 66 products; with _page_size=20 page 4 is the last. The pagination object contains ONLY previous_page — next_page is omitted entirely, not set to null as the spec's Pagination schema implies. Response body trimmed to the first 2 of 6 records.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products?_page_size=20&_page=4&_fields=sku
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [
            {
              "id": "6a38f615c3d65a5f868b1a39",
              "sku": "TSH-11470-W-M"
            },
            {
              "id": "6a38f615c3d65a5f868b1a3a",
              "sku": "TSH-11470-W-S"
            }
          ],
          "errors": [],
          "pagination": {
            "previous_page": "http://pim.dev.plytix.com/api/v3/products?_page_size=20&_page=3&_fields=sku"
          }
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: 200 - Single-Page Result Set (pagination is an empty object)
  description: Confirmed live 2026-10-01. When the whole result set fits on one page, pagination is {} — neither key is present. Same result for _page_size=500 over the full 66-product set.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products?sku=BAG-10157&_fields=sku
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [
            {
              "id": "6a38f614c3d65a5f868b1a06",
              "sku": "BAG-10157"
            }
          ],
          "errors": [],
          "pagination": {}
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: 422 - Pagination Bounds (_page >= 1, _page_size <= 1000)
  description: Confirmed live 2026-10-01. _page=0 and _page=-1 both produce the response below; _page_size=1001 and above produce "query._page_size: Input should be less than or equal to 1000". These are the only query params in this project found to carry explicit server-side bounds.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products?_page=0&_page_size=2&_fields=sku
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 422
      text: Unprocessable Entity
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [],
          "errors": [
            {
              "name": "InputDTOValidationError",
              "description": "query._page: Input should be greater than or equal to 1"
            }
          ]
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: 401 - Following next_page Verbatim Drops Auth
  description: Confirmed live 2026-10-01. pagination.next_page is an http:// URL. Requesting it as given returns 301 to https://pim.dev.plytix.com:443/..., and clients that do not forward Authorization across a scheme-changing redirect (plain curl -L, many SDK defaults) then get the 401 below. curl -L --location-trusted, or rewriting the scheme to https, returns 200 with the expected page.

  request: {
    url: http://pim.dev.plytix.com/api/v3/products?_page_size=2&_page=2&_fields=sku
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 401
      text: Unauthorized
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "detail": "Unauthorized"
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: 200 - Pagination (_page / _page_size)
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-07. _page_size=2 returns exactly 2 items; pagination.next_page contains _page=2 and preserves all other query params. Note: _offset/_limit returns 400 InvalidFieldError and is not supported.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products?_fields=id&_fields=sku&_page=1&_page_size=2
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [
            {
              "id": "6a38f614c3d65a5f868b1a06",
              "sku": "BAG-10157"
            },
            {
              "id": "6a38f614c3d65a5f868b1a07",
              "sku": "BAG-10158"
            }
          ],
          "errors": [],
          "pagination": {
            "next_page": "https://pim.dev.plytix.com/api/v3/products?_fields=id&_fields=sku&_page=2&_page_size=2"
          }
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: 200 - Full Parameters
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-22. Combines every confirmed-working query parameter dialect in one request for OpenAPI-example purposes -- five _fields entries, _page/_page_size, _sort_by, a plain field filter (status=Draft) and an operator filter (created[gt]=2024-01-01) together. All compose without conflict.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products?_fields=id&_fields=sku&_fields=label&_fields=status&_fields=created&_page=1&_page_size=5&_sort_by=sku&status=Draft&created[gt]=2024-01-01
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [
            {
              "id": "6aa022262b6fd055ffb7caa4",
              "sku": "WC-TEST-FULL-001",
              "label": "WC Test Full Product",
              "status": "Draft",
              "created": "2026-09-08T14:56:38.319000"
            },
            {
              "id": "6ab2fa2b125f1d0ceeeed6b3",
              "sku": "WC-TEST-MAXPARAMS-PARENT",
              "label": "WC Test Max Params Parent",
              "status": "Draft",
              "created": "2026-09-22T21:59:07.781000"
            }
          ],
          "errors": [],
          "pagination": {}
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: 200 - Full Parameters (Relationship Fields Expanded)
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-23. _fields=categories&_fields=assets&_fields=static_lists combined against BAG-10157, which has 2 real categories, 11 real assets, and 1 real static list membership ("All Products", an account-level default list). This is the CONFIRMED CORRECT way to get expanded relationship data for a product -- the equivalent dedicated subpaths (GET /products/{id}/categories, .../assets, .../static_lists) are all confirmed BROKEN as of 2026-09-23, always returning an empty array regardless of real linkage (see "Get Product Subpath - Attributes.bru" for the full writeup and captured broken-subpath examples). assets array trimmed from 11 to 2 entries here for brevity -- full entries share the same shape.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products?_fields=sku&_fields=categories&_fields=assets&_fields=static_lists&sku=BAG-10157
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [
            {
              "id": "6a38f614c3d65a5f868b1a06",
              "sku": "BAG-10157",
              "assets": [
                {
                  "id": "6a38f5e1c3d65a5f868b18a5",
                  "account_id": "6a38f5a5b22478f30bfd755c",
                  "assigned": true,
                  "content_type": "image/jpeg",
                  "extension": "jpg",
                  "file_size": 559164,
                  "file_type": "IMAGES",
                  "filename": "BAG-10157_10.jpg",
                  "path": "public_files/pim/assets/a5/f5/38/6a/6a38f5a5b22478f30bfd755c/images/e1/f5/38/6a/6a38f5e1c3d65a5f868b18a5/BAG-10157_10.jpg",
                  "n_catalogs": 0,
                  "n_products": 1,
                  "alt_text": null,
                  "status": "ACTIVE",
                  "created": "2026-06-22T08:44:19.008000",
                  "modified": "2026-06-22T08:44:19.046000"
                },
                {
                  "id": "6a38f5e1c3d65a5f868b18a6",
                  "account_id": "6a38f5a5b22478f30bfd755c",
                  "assigned": true,
                  "content_type": "image/jpeg",
                  "extension": "jpg",
                  "file_size": 798520,
                  "file_type": "IMAGES",
                  "filename": "BAG-10157_11.jpg",
                  "path": "public_files/pim/assets/a5/f5/38/6a/6a38f5a5b22478f30bfd755c/images/e1/f5/38/6a/6a38f5e1c3d65a5f868b18a6/BAG-10157_11.jpg",
                  "n_catalogs": 0,
                  "n_products": 1,
                  "alt_text": null,
                  "status": "ACTIVE",
                  "created": "2026-06-22T08:44:18.978000",
                  "modified": "2026-06-22T08:44:18.990000"
                }
              ],
              "categories": [
                {
                  "id": "6a38f5d8c3d65a5f868b185b",
                  "account_id": "6a38f5a5b22478f30bfd755c",
                  "name": "Backpacks",
                  "parent_id": "6a38f5d8c3d65a5f868b1856",
                  "path": ["Website Taxonomy", "Bags & Luggage", "Backpacks"],
                  "slug": "backpacks",
                  "order": 1,
                  "n_children": 0,
                  "created": "2026-06-22T08:44:08.298000",
                  "modified": "2026-06-22T08:44:08.298000"
                },
                {
                  "id": "6a38f5d8c3d65a5f868b1868",
                  "account_id": "6a38f5a5b22478f30bfd755c",
                  "name": "Backpacks",
                  "parent_id": "6a38f5d8c3d65a5f868b1830",
                  "path": ["Google Shopping Taxonomy", "Luggage & Bags", "Backpacks"],
                  "slug": "backpacks",
                  "order": 2,
                  "n_children": 0,
                  "created": "2026-06-22T08:44:08.300000",
                  "modified": "2026-06-22T08:44:08.300000"
                }
              ],
              "static_lists": [
                {
                  "id": "6a38f613c3d65a5f868b19fe",
                  "account_id": "6a38f5a5b22478f30bfd755c",
                  "name": "All Products",
                  "query": [[{"operator": "in", "field": "static_lists", "value": ["6a38f613c3d65a5f868b19fe"], "field_type": "PimProductAttribute.ObjectIdAttribute"}]],
                  "created": "2026-06-22T08:45:07.936000",
                  "modified": "2026-06-22T08:45:07.948000"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "errors": [],
          "pagination": {}
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: 200 - Plain Field Filter (sku)
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-07. sku=BAG-10157 returns exactly one matching product; pagination.next_page is null when the result set is exhausted. Operator (created[gt]=...) and related-entity dot (categories.name=Backpacks) filters also confirmed working in the same query-string dialect.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products?_fields=id&_fields=sku&sku=BAG-10157
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [
            {
              "id": "6a38f614c3d65a5f868b1a06",
              "sku": "BAG-10157"
            }
          ],
          "errors": [],
          "pagination": {
            "next_page": null
          }
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}
